// Reviewer correction: switched from GroundAoe's `pooled_debuff` (instant,
// non-lingering) to `StaticAura` (see transmutation/plant_growth.ron and
// axiomancy/magnify_gravity.ron, both already delivering `DifficultTerrain`
// this same way), which leaves a real, reapplying zone behind at the
// caster's position for `aura_duration`. `DifficultTerrain` ("slick
// footing... delivered by an aura", common/src/comp/buff.rs) is the closest
// already-shipped primitive to "slippery ground"; the sheet's secondary
// "possible prone on a failed save" is still dropped -- no
// knockdown-on-condition-failure primitive exists independent of an actual
// knockback attack effect, which this zone doesn't carry. `StaticAura`
// always places the zone at the caster's own position (no aimed placement
// exists, common/src/states/static_aura.rs) -- the sheet's 18 m cast range
// isn't mechanically expressed, the same simplification the two cited
// precedents already ship with.
StaticAura(
    buildup_duration: 0.5,
    cast_duration: 0.4,
    recover_duration: 0.35,
    energy_cost: 30.0,
    targets: OutOfGroup,
    auras: [
        (kind: DifficultTerrain, strength: 0.4, duration: Some(2), category: Some(Magical)),
    ],
    aura_duration: Some(10.0),
    range: 3.0,
    sprite_info: None,
    meta: (school: Some(Conjuration), source: Some(Arcane)),
)
